, "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9e14c34f-052a-4391-953c-de2971e14821", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836664.8187013, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8328df01-becc-4a85-8354-5f63ced5025e", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836664.8223145, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "d2e41603-5454-4b32-be4c-907de16b3260", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836665.573514, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8bc41b08-b3f0-4d32-9f51-d4e780d2f1fd", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836669.0207005, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a78bbdea-899b-4585-95eb-3711f17a25f6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836669.785363, "updated_at": 1789836684.621157, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — you absolutely have viable **$25–$45/month** options that fit the U.S./Mexico + eSIM + BYO Android model. I’d structure this as a decision tree:\n\n- **First choice: T-Mobile Keep & Switch**, because if Spectrum qualifies and your phone/device-financing paperwork clears, T-Mobile can reimburse up to **$800 per line** via virtual prepaid Mastercard after you port and submit proof. T-Mobile says the device financing must generally be at least 90 days old with at least three successful minimum payments, and the reimbursement typically takes about 15 days after submission. citeturn664719search0turn664719search4\n- **If T-Mobile falls through: Visible+ is probably the cleanest fit for your use case.** Current promo pricing is **$29/month**, taxes/fees included, with unlimited talk/text/data in Mexico and Canada and **2 GB of high-speed data per day** while roaming there, then reduced speeds. Visible+ Pro is **$39/month** with more perks, but you probably don’t need it. citeturn664719search5\n- **US Mobile is the flexibility play.** Unlimited Starter is **$25/month** taxes/fees included, but monthly Starter does **not** include the same meaningful Mexico roaming bucket by default; you can add roaming, or use their North America by-the-gig setup. Their Premium plan gives up to **20 GB international roaming** and costs more. US Mobile also supports eSIM and multiple underlying networks, which is nice if you want carrier flexibility. citeturn609988search7turn609988search8turn664719search1\n- **AT&T Prepaid is the boring but solid fallback.** Their current **Unlimited Enhanced Plus is $45/month** and explicitly includes Mexico and Canada use, with unlimited talk/text/data and 10 GB hotspot. citeturn609988search5\n- **Google Fi works well internationally, but it misses your price target for one line.** Unlimited Premium is **$65/month** and gives broad international coverage; Unlimited Standard has Canada/Mexico support but is priced better mostly when you have multiple lines. citeturn664719search6\n\nFor what you actually described — **one line, U.S. + Mexico, eSIM, Android, solid data, around $40 or less** — I’d narrow it to:\n\n**1. T-Mobile**, if they pay off Spectrum.  \n**2. Visible+ at ~$29**, if you want the simplest low-cost U.S./Mexico setup.  \n**3. US Mobile**, if you want more control over network choice and roaming configuration.  \n**4. AT&T Prepaid at $45**, if you want mainstream-carrier simplicity and don’t mind being slightly above target.\n\nAnd because you’re planning to spend real time in Playa, one technical point matters: **Mexico roaming terms are often built for travel, not permanent majority-of-use in Mexico.** So before we lock anything, we should specifically check each carrier’s long-term roaming/fair-use rule. That’s the next thing I’d compare, because it matters more for you than headline price. citeturn664719search7\n\nIf you want, I can do the next pass specifically as **“best plan for living in Mexico but keeping a U.S. number”** and strip out anything that’s really only good for short trips.", "text_chars": 3081, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e78b2d31-ce4e-4999-83e8-ffe416c4b0ac", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836671.601898, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "fdb88647-8e9e-4216-86b0-457827892fce", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836671.642582, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "db1a828d-880e-421f-b41d-df988764c23c", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836714.178941, "updated_at": 1789836745.60734, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I thought about Visible. Now, I want to find a phone, like a OnePlus, older version Snapdragon, at a pawn shop. So I'm going to start looking and I— my budget's 100 bucks. That should get us a value phone, for two, three hundred bucks. Can you give me some options? Remember, it's got to be eSIM compatible, go back and forth from Mexico, New York. And again, I say good data, but not this. I get 10 gigabytes a month and then it gets capped. What are my options?", "text_chars": 469, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a50c464a-c734-4ff4-bbb8-218d4bf1b147", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836717.338423, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "f3c5acc1-12f8-4119-9601-a86d706251c4", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836719.8420293, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "c37b9b19-72ea-4221-93e4-745681b6f149", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836719.8461494, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "6fec3722-510f-4ea3-97e0-528be29dba32", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836720.701774, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "af35cae1-64b9-4737-82b2-dbd5ded7a2d3", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1789836726.0216305, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "d1a768ad-e3c8-403c-82ea-d0822346a58e", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836727.136239, "updated_at": 1789844225.071046, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — with a hard **$100 pawn-shop target**, I would not make OnePlus the only target. The eSIM requirement narrows the field a lot, and older OnePlus support is inconsistent. For example, the **OnePlus 12R does not support eSIM** on the official spec page, so we need to verify exact model numbers before buying. citeturn651007search7turn651007search10\n\nThe cleaner used-phone targets are:\n\n| Phone | Why it fits | Pawn target |\n|---|---|---:|\n| **Google Pixel 6a** | eSIM + physical SIM, 5G, broad U.S./Mexico bands, Wi-Fi 6E | **$80–120** |\n| **Google Pixel 7** | newer, better modem/camera, eSIM + physical SIM | **$120–170** |\n| **OnePlus 11 5G** | Snapdragon 8 Gen 2, still current enough for OxygenOS 16, strong performance | **$150–220** |\n| **Samsung S22** | Snapdragon in U.S. model, eSIM support, strong carrier compatibility | **$140–200** |\n| **Samsung S23 FE / S23** | better long-term support, eSIM, strong U.S./Mexico carrier fit | **$180–250** |\n\nFor **$100 specifically**, the **Pixel 6a is probably the sweet spot**. Google confirms it supports **dual SIM with nano-SIM + eSIM**, and the U.S. model has a broad LTE/5G band set including bands useful on U.S. networks and Mexico. citeturn651007search1turn651007search2\n\nThe OnePlus route is still good if you find the right one. I’d target a **OnePlus 11 5G, North American model CPH2451**, because that model is still getting current OxygenOS updates. citeturn651007search8 I would **not buy any OnePlus at a pawn shop until we confirm the exact model number and eSIM menu**.\n\nFor your service, since you said **10 GB/month is enough**, you do not necessarily need an expensive unlimited plan. A few workable structures are:\n\n- **AT&T Prepaid 8 GB / 3-month plan:** about **$33/month**, and it explicitly works in the **U.S., Mexico, and Canada** with the same 8 GB bucket. After 8 GB, speeds drop to 128 Kbps. citeturn242784search9\n- **AT&T Prepaid Unlimited Enhanced Plus:** **$45/month**, Mexico/Canada included, unlimited domestic data and 10 GB hotspot. citeturn242784search8\n- **Visible:** starts around **$25/month** for unlimited U.S. data, but I would only use it for your Mexico plan after confirming the exact roaming tier and IMEI compatibility. Visible explicitly warns that not every BYOD Android works on its network, so we need to run the pawn-shop IMEI before buying. citeturn242784search4turn242784search10\n- **US Mobile:** flexible, but Mexico roaming on the cheaper tiers is more piecemeal; their add-ons are **$15 for 1 GB** or **$30 for 5 GB**, while Premium includes much more international roaming. citeturn242784search1turn242784search3\n\nFor your exact use case, I’d hunt in this order: **Pixel 6a first, Pixel 7 second, OnePlus 11 if we get lucky, Samsung S22 as another strong fallback.**\n\nAt the pawn shop, before handing them a dollar, check four things: **unlocked, clean IMEI, EID present under `*#06#`, and battery/USB-C condition**. AT&T specifically says an **EID** is the quick confirmation that the device can use eSIM. citeturn242784search5\n\nIf you send me photos/model numbers from the pawn shop, I can tell you **buy / pass** on each one in real time.", "text_chars": 3188, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d5f21bd3-e6e6-4bc5-8927-d72f6a76ecb4", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789836731.283136, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "48d3