necessary.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Project Brief — Vegas Liquidity & Stay Operations\n\n### Project name\n\n**Vegas Liquidity & Stay Operations**\n\n### Mission\n\nMaintain continuous lodging, food, connectivity, and work capability while minimizing locked cash and eliminating emergency hotel scrambling.\n\nThis project should externalize all hotel dates, holds, release timing, resort credits, cash injections, and known future liquidity gaps.\n\n### Core doctrine\n\n**Cash ≠ holds ≠ expected inflows ≠ promo value.**\n\nEvery update must preserve those categories.\n\n### Project board\n\nUse five lanes:\n\n**1. Cash**\n- bank balance\n- physical cash\n- confirmed posted inflows\n\n**2. Holds**\n- hotel\n- amount\n- check-in\n- checkout\n- expected release\n- actual release\n\n**3. Stay Calendar**\n- hotel\n- dates\n- room cost\n- deposit/hold\n- booking status\n\n**4. Non-Cash Value**\n- resort credit\n- free play\n- dining credit\n- amount used\n- remaining\n\n**5. Future Gates**\n- next hotel requiring new cash\n- upcoming known inflows\n- unresolved timing risks\n- projected liquidity gap\n\n### Rules for the project\n\n1. **Never double count money.**\n2. Pending authorization = locked, not spendable.\n3. Expected refund = $0 until posted.\n4. Free play = $0 until converted.\n5. Resort credit never counts as cash.\n6. Use clean-folio settlement data from actual MGM stays as the preferred timing model.\n7. Maintain one canonical hotel calendar.\n8. Any hotel-plan change must update:\n   - dates\n   - room cost\n   - hold\n   - expected release date\n   - downstream liquidity\n9. Always identify the **next funding gate**.\n10. Optimize only after lodging continuity is protected.\n\n### Standard update format\n\nWhenever Peter gives a new balance, hold, booking, or payment, respond with:\n\n**Now**\n- hard cash\n- locked holds\n- non-cash value\n\n**Next move**\n- next hotel\n- required cash\n- expected release/inflow before then\n\n**After move**\n- estimated liquid balance\n- next risk/gate\n\nDo not rebuild the entire history unless asked.\n\n### Current project checkpoint\n\n**Stable through Monday Sept. 21.**\n\nImmediate sequence:\n\n**Luxor → Monday Excalibur one-night bridge → Tuesday Excalibur two-night block → Sept. 24 Luxor King Suite**\n\nThe major strategic objective is to transition from daily $50–150 bridge management into a larger stable liquidity cushion before October.\n\nThe next significant future funding gate is **Fontainebleau on Oct. 12**.\n\n---\n\nThat should be enough to cleanly leave this chat. I’d paste **Part 1 into the new personal chat** and **Part 2 into the project instructions**.", "text_chars": 9921, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f0aeb886-fd47-4e16-a14b-346d8073a25e", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789931019.225633, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4dbf0840-38c5-445c-bf9a-ae5b2e44fa8d", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789931779.432205, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "656e552b-fdde-4e5d-b429-38719bbe5c0c", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789931779.953316, "updated_at": 1789931783.839972, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "mu