ry, sleep/energy questions only  \n**Do not mix in:** Vegas cash flow, hotel holds, jobs, ATEX, relocation, phone, or GCE unless directly relevant to the health question.\n\n## Current health / wellness baseline\n\nThe standing health framework is built around a sustainable rhythm of **food, exercise, focus, and recovery**, with intake adjusted to actual hunger, energy, sleep, workload, and health needs. The prior plan was intentionally simple: a basic breakfast, one satiating anchor meal, hydration, and additional food when needed rather than rigid restriction. fileciteturn18file1L11-L16 fileciteturn18file1L39-L44\n\n### Nutrition pattern\n\nThe established grocery baseline centers on:\n\n- **Pea protein**\n- **Avocados**\n- **Chia / flax / hemp seed blend**\n- **Eggs or cheese**\n- **Electrolytes as needed**\n- Tuna/sardines or other practical protein as optional additions rather than mandatory staples. fileciteturn18file1L52-L61\n\nA practical meal rhythm previously used was **avocado + eggs + protein shake** in the morning, with another small protein/whole-food buffer meal if work made a full meal difficult, followed by one inexpensive real meal later. The protein powder was explicitly meant as portable support, **not a replacement for all whole food**. fileciteturn18file1L66-L71\n\nThe later executed grocery baseline included **365 Organic Pea Protein, Super Seed Trio, avocados, cheddar, and electrolyte sticks**. fileciteturn18file1L76-L84\n\n### Exercise / movement\n\nThe original plan used **walking as the default exercise and transportation**, with bodyweight work, hotel gyms, swimming, or structured walks as additional low-cost activity. At the time that artifact was written, the documented comfortable walking range was approximately **2–3 miles**, so any newer mileage or tolerance should supersede that older baseline rather than be assumed unchanged. fileciteturn18file1L29-L33\n\n### Recovery / daily rhythm\n\nThe intended daily structure was:\n\n**simple breakfast → focused work block → filling meal → walking/workout → recovery/decompression**\n\nThe plan specifically called out **energy, sleep, hunger, workload, and health** as variables that should modify the routine rather than forcing the routine regardless of how the body is responding. fileciteturn18file1L34-L44\n\n## Current real-world update from this chat\n\nThe older Drive plan is now partly stale because hotel living has continued for several more weeks. The important current update is that food has become repetitive and restaurant-heavy, and the upcoming **Vdara stay provides a proper kitchen and full refrigerator**. The intended health use of that stay is to return to **groceries, cooking, and meal prep for several days** rather than continuing sandwiches/tater tots/takeout.\n\nThat is a lifestyle update from this conversation, not something documented in the older Drive artifact.\n\n## What the Drive material does *not* establish\n\nThe Drive material I found does **not** document a diagnosis, prescription-medication list, recent laboratory results, blood pressure history, physician assessment, chronic disease, or a specific active symptom workup.\n\nSo the next health chat should **not infer any of those**. Start from whatever current health question you bring in and distinguish clearly between:\n- what you report now,\n- what the older wellness artifact documents,\n- and any medical guidance or evidence we add afterward.\n\n## New-chat boot line\n\n**Health lane only. Use “Vegas Food, Exercise, and Daily Rhythm — Living Plan” as historical wellness context, not as a medical record. Current known baseline: protein/whole-food-oriented eating pattern, walking and light exercise as primary activity, hydration/electrolytes as needed, and an upcoming return to grocery cooking/meal prep after prolonged hotel eating. Do not import Vegas finances, hotels, jobs, ATEX, relocation, phone planning, or GCE unless directly relevant. Do n